{"id": "EUVD-2026-59459", "enisaUuid": "f7425c8b-c152-34d3-84ef-d9a0a320e464", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nvhost/vdpa: validate virtqueue index in mmap and fault paths\n\nvhost_vdpa_mmap() and vhost_vdpa_fault() use vma->vm_pgoff as a\nvirtqueue index for get_vq_notification(), but they do not validate\nthat the index is smaller than v->nvqs.\n\nThe ioctl path already performs both a bounds check and\narray_index_nospec(), but the mmap/fault path only checks that the\nindex fits in u16. This allows an out-of-range queue index to reach\ndriver-specific get_vq_notification() callbacks.\n\nFix this by extracting a unified vhost_vdpa_get_vq_notification()\nhelper that validates the queue index against v->nvqs and applies\narray_index_nospec() before calling the driver callback. Both the\nmmap and fault paths use this helper, and the bounds checking is\nconsolidated into a single location.\n\nFrom source inspection, the most defensible impact is out-of-bounds\naccess in the callback path, potentially leading to invalid PFN\nremaps and crash/DoS.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:58:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:32", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f310bac6db9bd3bb1655707d692d9d2a86eeb17", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4bf5a51963ff816f7443702dc536b9327cf5e550", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/55a644031e610ea93fbde2702c7b8f267476552f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2b3f79b90b231a682315fe2191bb71925650e183", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bbba4f92515238d76018e9b75e41b16d83df52c8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f5f94c6c6b2e4eaa5b45815509e21d0c6cfa81e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/32ac9097aa2463fcfc12f61cc4a9ebc3579cba7d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/929e4f044621c8cc30b612fb74e1410bef09e41b"], "aliases": ["GHSA-vx5g-7fcv-7h84", "CVE-2026-74312"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08f6af75-3b43-3b4c-a6da-8f26c6b25d9f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddd89d0a059d8e9740c75a97e0efe9bf07ee51f9 <1f5f94c6c6b2e4eaa5b45815509e21d0c6cfa81e"}, {"id": "228a9c3f-cb89-3bbd-abfa-0d41fb492173", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "2829fc7e-93b8-3a6a-8c8b-5918b80a480d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddd89d0a059d8e9740c75a97e0efe9bf07ee51f9 <bbba4f92515238d76018e9b75e41b16d83df52c8"}, {"id": "2f77da6e-8093-39dc-b531-82139266a16a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.261"}, {"id": "34622c8f-37ce-392a-a645-9f0348981032", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.212"}, {"id": "58962528-2b11-3edd-a0cf-deacc9a09cc0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.178"}, {"id": "672b6d67-0ea3-31fa-863a-11280edb6a08", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.8"}, {"id": "6bd177ce-a985-3661-bb60-5b3853f5062f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "6ea9a684-8146-3cdf-a043-f97caabb8aff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddd89d0a059d8e9740c75a97e0efe9bf07ee51f9 <0f310bac6db9bd3bb1655707d692d9d2a86eeb17"}, {"id": "878e6301-1867-35e5-b09f-15cb4e5de21b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ddd89d0a059d8e9740c75a97e0efe9bf07ee51f9 <32ac9097aa2463fcfc12f61cc4a9ebc3579cba7d"}, {"id": "a5b3a779-5bc9-3446-a87f-ce118e467aeb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a7cb5c15-7470-39a5-a29f-d665837c8556", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_vers